# iPix Mintlify

Search existing canonical pages before creating a file. Update in place. Do not duplicate PRDs, roadmaps, or architecture.

Content root is the **git repo root**. Keep `.mintignore` excluding `app/`, `src/`, `docs/`, `supabase/`, and other non-Mintlify trees. Do not ignore shipping MDX, `docs.json`, or `favicon.svg`.

## Do not create empty docs

```text
real feature → canonical documentation → navigation entry
```

Never add a page whose body is "Content coming soon" (or equivalent). If there is nothing true to write, do not add the nav entry. Do not list paths in `docs.json` that have no MDX file (`ai/agents`, `ai/workflows`, `ai/model-providers` were this bug).

Empty tabs stay out of `docs.json` (hide by omission). Files on disk can remain; nav is the product surface.

## Information architecture

Start Here → Core → MVP → Advanced → Planning → Reference → Archive.

Do not bulk-move folders or prefix URLs with `00-`, `01-`, etc. Keep existing paths unless a later wave explicitly migrates them.

Do not fill a technology tab just because it exists. Do not write Advanced docs for features that are not in the product yet. Do not import `docs/` planning markdown wholesale into Mintlify.

`/` redirects to `/overview/ipix`. Do not add a second `index.mdx` Start Here.

## Document types (one owner)

| Type | Owns |
|---|---|
| Start Here / architecture | How an operator starts; how the system fits |
| PRD | What and why |
| Roadmap | When |
| Audit | Dated evidence — never a product overview |
| Linear issue | One executable unit |
| Reference | Stable lookup |

Keep audits out of product sidebars (CopilotKit, Brand Hub, etc.). Put them under Planning or Archive with a date in the title.

## Mintlify mechanics

- Every shipped page: `title` and `description` frontmatter. Use `sidebarTitle` when the nav label should be shorter.
- Internal links: root-relative, no `.mdx` suffix (`/overview/architecture`).
- Use Mintlify components (`Note`, `Tip`, `Steps`, `Card`, `Warning`).
- Mermaid fenced blocks for flows; one canonical diagram per topic.
- Verify claims against `app/` and `supabase/`. No secrets. No `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` AI keys.
- After nav or MDX changes: `mint validate` and `mint broken-links` at repo root.

## PRs

Mintlify content is docs-only. Do not mix with production app code in the same PR (AGENTS.md #1).
When architecture, schema, AI contracts, or operator journeys change, update the canonical Mintlify page in the docs PR.
